\fs32\b The Grid\b0\fs20\par
\par
The transcription grid is the main working area in WinBMD2. Each row represents an entry from the index and each column represents one item of information to be transcribed.\par
\par
\fs24\b Moving around the grid\b0\fs20\par
Use Tab or Enter to move to the next field while transcribing.\par
\par
Use Shift+Tab to move back to the previous field.\par
\par
The mouse and the normal navigation keys can also be used when you need to move directly to another part of the grid.\par
\par
\fs24\b Horizontal and vertical entry\b0\fs20\par
WinBMD2 supports both horizontal and vertical entry modes.\par
\par
In horizontal mode, transcription proceeds across the fields of one entry before moving to the next entry.\par
\par
In vertical mode, transcription proceeds down a column before moving to the next field.\par
\par
The preferred entry mode can be selected in Options.\par
\par
\fs24\b Entering and editing information\b0\fs20\par
Select a field and type the information shown on the scan. Existing information can be edited whenever a correction is required.\par
\par
WinBMD2 may provide automatic completion, picklists or validation depending on the field being edited.\par
\par
\fs24\b Copying information from the previous entry\b0\fs20\par
Where appropriate, WinBMD2 can copy information from the entry above when moving into an empty field. This is useful for information which is repeated over several consecutive entries.\par
\par
Always check automatically copied information against the scan.\par
\par
\fs24\b Surnames\b0\fs20\par
When consecutive entries have the same surname, WinBMD2 can reduce repeated typing by carrying the surname forward where appropriate.\par
\par
The behaviour of automatic surname copying can be changed in Options.\par
\par
\fs24\b Column widths\b0\fs20\par
Grid columns can be resized to suit the information being transcribed and the available screen space.\par
\par
WinBMD2 remembers column widths so that the grid can be restored to a useful layout when the program is used again.\par
\par
\fs24\b Validation\b0\fs20\par
Fields are checked as information is entered. WinBMD2 may warn when a value is missing, unusual or does not have the expected format.\par
\par
Validation is intended to help find possible transcription mistakes. When an unusual value really does appear on the index, transcribe what is shown on the scan.\par
\par
\fs24\b Picklists\b0\fs20\par
Forenames and registration districts can display picklists containing likely values. These allow common entries to be selected with less typing.\par
\par
Picklist and automatic-completion behaviour can be changed in Options.\par
\par
\fs24\b Verification state\b0\fs20\par
Rows which have been changed may need to be verified again. This ensures that information altered after verification is checked against the scan before the transcription is completed.\par
\par
See the Verification topic for more information.\par
\par
\fs24\b Directives\b0\fs20\par
Some transcription files contain directive lines rather than ordinary index entries. Directives are used to provide special instructions within a transcription and are entered differently from normal index entries.\par
\par
{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "winbmdhelp://directives"}}{\fldrslt{\ul More about Directives...}}}\par
\par
